 "run": "2026-10-14, CPU, tools/shaders/dither_temporal.mjs, the protocol committed first (5665ad0)",
 "findings": [
  "Pan and game (moving content, steady light): the mix modes flicker least. PICO-8 pan: mix-bayer4 0.230, bayer4 0.245, blue 0.255, none 0.260. PICO-8 game: mix-bayer4 0.115, bayer4 0.121.",
  "Lamp (static camera, light flickering about 8%): the mix modes flicker most, about 2.8 times bayer4 on PICO-8 (0.568 against 0.204) and EGA (0.808 against 0.284), and toggle 3.7 to 4.7 times as many pixels. A small change in colour reorders the 16-entry plan, so many pixels change entry at once. This is the weakness the mix-runs file predicted.",
  "Fade (slow exposure ramp): mix-bayer4 flickers more than bayer4 on PICO-8 (0.206 against 0.143) and about the same on EGA (0.217 against 0.215).",
  "mix-bayer8 gives the same indices as mix-bayer4 on every frame (0 of 76,800 differ, checked). Cause: the plan has 16 entries and the pick is floor(16 t); the 8 x 8 Bayer matrix is 4 times the 4 x 4 matrix plus a 2 x 2 term below 4, so floor(16 t) recovers the 4 x 4 index exactly. The mode is redundant as built.",
  "Still accuracy (error) agrees with the mix-runs file: the mix modes are 2.5 to 7 times closer to the source."
 ],
 "does_not_prove": "Flicker as people see it (the 4 x 4 box stands in for the eye); palettes beyond PICO-8 and EGA; GPU behaviour beyond the exact index parity already in evidence."
}
